  "question": {
    "text": "The equation <math><mo>|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo></math> represents:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "a circle of radius <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "a circle of radius <math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "the line through the origin with slope <math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "the line through the origin with slope <math><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0139_9679b4105213.png\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br />Hence, the equation represents a line through the origin with slope <math><mn>1</mn></math> .</p>"
  }
